     </widget>
     <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="plainTextEdit_7">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>130</x>
        <y>90</y>
        <width>481</width>
        <height>311</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="styleSheet">
       <string notr="true">background: transparent;
border: transparent;
font: 500 italic 10pt &quot;aakra&quot;;</string>
      </property>
      <property name="plainText">
       <string>If there is not enough,
a vote is held to determine who will be deprived
of water. After the vote, only a
number of players equal to the number of available
water rations will be allowed to remain. The others
tragically die of thirst, and leave the game.

B. Consuming Food (Fish marker):
Once the water rations have been “distributed”, the players are ready
to consume food.
If there are at least as many rations of food as there are survivors,
subtract 1 ration for each survivor, and the round ends.

If there is not enough, a vote
is held to determine who will be deprived of food. After the vote, only a number
of players equal to the number of available food
rations will be allowed to remain. The others
tragically die of hunger, and leave the game.</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
    </widget>
    <widget class="QWidget" name="rules_4">
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">background-image: url(:/pap_wood-1.jpg);</string>
     </property>
     <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="plainTextEdit_3">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>130</x>
        <y>90</y>
        <width>481</width>
        <height>311</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="styleSheet">
       <string notr="true">background: transparent;
border: transparent;
font: 500 italic 10pt &quot;aakra&quot;;</string>
      </property>
      <property name="readOnly">
       <bool>true</bool>
      </property>
      <property name="plainText">
       <string>5. Check for game end
After any votes, and adjusting the markers according to the number
of rations consumed, check to see if the game ends. If not, the surviving players begin a new round with
the First Player card passing to the right.

1. Catch Fish
When you choose this action, draw a ball from the bag. The number
of fish on the ball (1 ,2 ,3 ) indicates how many fish you
caught. Advance the Food marker that many spaces
on the survival track on the board. Then return the ball to the bag.

2. Collect water
When you choose this action, look at the number in the water
droplet on the Weather card for this turn (it will range from 0 to 3)
and advance the Water marker (Droplet ) that many spaces on the
survival track on the board. Note that you cannot collect any water
on an extremely sunny day (when the droplet depicts 0 0 ): so be
careful and plan for it!</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
