     <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="plainTextEdit_8">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>130</x>
        <y>90</y>
        <width>481</width>
        <height>311</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="styleSheet">
       <string notr="true">background: transparent;
border: transparent;
font: 500 italic 10pt &quot;aakra&quot;;</string>
      </property>
      <property name="plainText">
       <string>Whether you are bitten by a snake or succeed in
collecting more wood, return the balls to the bag.
The Wood disc will circulate around the Raft track
(from 0 to 6). As soon as it reaches the 6th space,
add a Raft card to the Raft card space, and move the
disc back to space 0. Each Raft card allows one surviving player to
escape the island 

Votes are necessary in the event of a water or food shortage
(or if the players must leave the island, but do not have enough seats
on the raft). everyone votes against another player by clicking on that player.
Whichever player has the most votes against him is eliminated.

While you are sick, you cannot vote at the end of this round (but of course
you can be eliminated), and you cannot take an action.
</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
    </widget>
    <widget class="QWidget" name="rules_7">
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">background-image: url(:/pap_wood-1.jpg);</string>
     </property>
     <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="plainTextEdit_5">
      <property name="geometry">
       <rect>
        <x>130</x>
        <y>90</y>
        <width>481</width>
        <height>311</height>
       </rect>
      </property>
      <property name="styleSheet">
       <string notr="true">background: transparent;
border: transparent;
font: 500 italic 10pt &quot;aakra&quot;;</string>
      </property>
      <property name="readOnly">
       <bool>true</bool>
      </property>
      <property name="plainText">
       <string>The game can end 3 ways:

Leaving the island
At the end of any round, the surviving players can board the raft. In
order to embark, the following conditions must be met:
• The water and food rations must have been distributed already.
• There must be at least as many Raft cards built as there are
survivors.
• There must be at least
1 ration of water and
food remaining for
each survivor (for
the Trip).

Example: There are 4 players remaining at the end of the round,
and the survival track indicates 8 water and 9 food. The players
distribute the food, reducing the supplies to 4 water and 5 food.
There are 4 Raft cards on the Raft card space on the board. The
4 players have everything they need to embark and win the game
(it is entirely possible for every player to survive and win).
</string>
      </property>
     </widget>
